v2.0.0 rebuilt the Baccarat module as a local Python server application, replacing a five-file
browser prototype that was reviewed and found not releasable.

v2.1.0 added a Tie bet alongside Banker or Player, moved the disclaimer to the foot of the window and
removed page scrolling. v2.2.x put the panels beside the betting column for half-screen use and gave
the bead plate a fixed 10 x 10 box. v2.3.0 made PASS record the table's result. v2.4.0 gave the Tie
insurance its own stake. v2.5.x built and proved the OCR tooling and prompt. v2.6.0 is where the reader
met the real table. v2.7.x added one-click calibration, gated Automatic behind a 0.9 confidence bar,
proved the live loop end to end and made an uncapturable region say so.

v2.8.0 is the milestone: the reader read the user's live casino display through their calibrated
region (12 of 12 decisive readings correct, including a Tie verified against the picture), found that
a region containing the history grid and the balance row made the model burn its whole token budget
(raising the budget did not help; cropping did), added a Draw-the-region button, and stopped
self-captured samples from "calibrating" a profile by matching themselves.

v2.8.1 closes the "why is no result showing?" traps: a whole-screen region is refused at Start with a
plain explanation, changing the profile while the reader runs is pointed out with the fix (Stop, then
Start), and a hand-drawn region no longer inherits a stale match score.

The per-release record for the module is BACARAT/CHANGELOG.md.
